      "text": "I don't have direct knowledge of a separate \"state editor\" interface with controls for demi-plane size, locations, or images. That kind of world-editing tool isn't something I can see or point you to from here.\n\nWhat I can tell you is what **I** have access to on my end for editing the current state:\n\n- **Locations/regions/areas** — I can create new areas and move the party around existing locations, and look up lore about places.\n- **NPCs** — I can create, edit, rename, reposition, or remove NPCs.\n- **Player characters** — I can edit attributes, skills, traits, abilities, backstory, resources (health, mana, stamina, reputation), inventory, and portraits.\n- **Travel/world layout** — I can see where the party is and where nearby places are.\n\nBut if you're asking about an in-app *visible editor* where **you** manually drag sliders for world size, place image tiles, or configure the demi-plane visually — that's not something I have visibility into. That would be part of the game's UI itself, not a tool exposed to me.\n\nIf you tell me what you're trying to change in the world (say, expanding the demi-plane's dimensions, adding a new location, or adjusting a map), I can make those changes through the tools I have. Want me to do that?",
