      "text": "You're laying out a map-tile scheme for the demi-plane. Let me make sure I'm tracking this correctly against the world data.\n\n**Tiles 01–05 (the −8 row):**\n01 The Dim March (−2,−8)\n02 The Grey Boundary (−1,−8)\n03 The Open Horizon (0,−8)\n04 The Fade (1,−8)\n05 The Last Edge (2,−8)\n\n**Tiles 06–10 (the −9 row):**\n06 The Low Reaches (−2,−9)\n07 The Hollow Vale (−1,−9)\n08 The Deep Expanse (0,−9)\n09 The Southroll (1,−9)\n10 The Rift March (2,−9)\n\n**Tiles 11–13 (the −10 row):**\n11 The Quiet Shore (−2,−10)\n12 The Westreach (−1,−10)\n13 Heartgate Basin (0,−10)\n\nTwo of those match regions that already exist in the world data:\n- **11 The Quiet Shore (−2,−10)** — matches the established **Quiet Shore** region exactly (coordinate −2,−10).\n- **12 The Westreach (−1,−10)** — matches the established **Westreach** region exactly (coordinate −1,−10).\n\nThe rest of your tiles (01–10 and 13) are regions that aren't yet recorded in the world data — the map tile at (0,−10) isn't yet named \"Heartgate Basin\" in the system, and your named regions there (the Dim March, the Grey Boundary, the Open Horizon, the Fade, the Last Edge, the Low Reaches, the Hollow Vale, the Deep Expanse, the Southroll, and the Rift March) don't exist as regions yet.\n\nSo the question is how you'd like to treat these. A few options:\n\n1. **Record the two matching tiles** (Quiet Shore, Westreach) as canonical, and treat the others as an extension project — naming and manifesting them as new regions.\n2. **Establish the full tile grid** as your map canon, creating the remaining regions (11 new ones) with those names and coordinates.\n3. **Something else** — if this tile list is meant to align differently with the existing regions (e.g., renaming or re-coordinating), let me know.\n\nWhat direction do you want me to take with these? And should I go ahead and register the full set as named regions in the demi-plane so the map matches the world?",
