    {
      "userId": "0",
      "username": "Narrator",
      "text": "You're right to catch that — let me explain what the data shows, because it's genuinely a bit inconsistent right now.\n\nThe system records your **realm as \"Demi-Plane\"**, and places you in **The Southroll** region — which is a *demi-plane region*, not an Aerfála region. Greenmeadow is registered as being in The Southroll at coordinates (−11, 1194).\n\nYou're right that **that doesn't make sense** narratively. In the story, you stepped through a torii gate into an actual forest in **Aerfála** — a silver-barked forest, a dirt road, then Greenmeadow village. That's very clearly *outer-world Aerfála*, not your demi-plane's golden Southroll. The Southroll is described as perpetual golden hills with fireflies and hill foxes — nothing like the spring meadow, timber-and-plaster village, and shaggy ponies you found.\n\nSo the mechanical tracking and the story have diverged. Two ways to read it:\n\n1. **The tracking is wrong** — the system conflated your demi-plane's Southroll region with the village, and Greenmeadow should actually be recorded as an **Aerfála** location, not part of your demi-plane at all. This matches the story you actually told.\n\n2. **The tracking is \"right\"** by the map project you were discussing earlier (the tile grid with \"The Southroll,\" \"Open Horizon,\" etc.), in which case Greenmeadow being placed in the Southroll is intentional — but that contradicts the story where you went *through the gate into Aerfála*.\n\nGiven the story, **option 1 is clearly what happened.** Greenmeadow is in Aerfála. The demi-plane's Southroll is a separate place you built (and haven't re-entered since stepping through the gate).\n\nSo — what I can't do is silently maintain two contradictory truths. I'd rather ask you: do you want me to treat **Greenmeadow as an Aerfála location** (correcting the record so the village is no longer parked inside your demi-plane region)? Or is your intent that this runs *inside* your demi-plane, in which case the story text for arriving here should have grounded that more explicitly?\n\nWhich way do you want it? I'll align the world data to match the story.",
