      "description": "A ceremonial jade coin minted by the Kitsune no Kage, bearing the household crest of the Mother Fox. Each coin is hand-carved from pale green jade with a fox-and-torii motif and a hole at center for cord threading. Within Tsukiko's estate and among those who formally recognize her authority, Jade Rite Coins function as sanctioned tokens for estate business: ritual offerings, hospitality payments, retainers' stipends, commissions, permissions, favors, and authorized trade. They are not legal tender in Aerfála's copper-silver-gold economy and carry no fixed universal exchange rate. Outside Tsukiko's sphere, their value is entirely social — merchants may refuse them, accept them as curiosities, or negotiate an ad-hoc gold equivalent. As Tsukiko's influence becomes known, certain traders, nobles, collectors, scholars, temples, mages, fox-kin, yokai, and diplomats may seek them deliberately for their rarity, craftsmanship, magical provenance, or association with the Mother Fox. Counterfeiting, hoarding, collecting, and speculation may emerge naturally as circulation widens. Knowledge of the coins cannot spread instantly — it must travel through believable contact, rumor, trade, witnessed use, or investigation.",
