      "x": 2,
      "y": 0,
      "basicInfo": "The Caelvir Forest Commune encompasses the continent's eastern ancient forest — a vast canopy of silver-barked elder trees whose roots predate every human kingdom. The elves of Caelvir govern through a Circle of Elders who speak for the forest itself, and their society runs on consensus, ritual, and the slow patience of long-lived people. Outsiders see a beautiful, inscrutable woodland; residents see a living organism with moods, preferences, and boundaries that must be respected. The forest's deeper regions hold spirit groves, healing springs, and ruins from ages when the elves ruled half the continent. Border settlements trade cautiously with outsiders — furs, herbs, enchanted wood — while keeping the heartwood closed to all but the Wardens. The forest is gorgeous, dangerous, and extremely opinionated about guests.",
