    "The Verdant Plot": {
      "areas": {
        "common-hall": {
          "description": "A central gathering space for the Demi-Plane's residents — currently modest but functional. A long table, a hearth that burns without fuel, and a board where the Chamberlain posts development proposals and chore assignments. Residents eat here, meet here, and argue about whose turn it is to tend the eastern orchard here. The hall grows as the settlement does — the Chamberlain has plans for expansion pinned to the wall.",
          "paths": [
            "farm-fields",
            "residential-row"
          ]
        },
        "farm-fields": {
          "description": "Soil has appeared where there was only flat stone. Rich, dark, and responsive — seeds placed here take root within hours. The fields stretch in neat rows that the Chamberlain organized, each one labeled with what is growing and when it was planted. Irrigation channels run between the rows, fed by a spring that appeared the moment someone wished for water.",
          "paths": [
            "common-hall"
          ]
        },
        "residential-row": {
          "description": "A cluster of small dwellings line a path leading away from the common hall. Each one is shaped by its occupant — a healer's cottage with drying herbs, a warrior's quarters with a weapon rack, a merchant's room with an inventory ledger. The architecture shifts to match whoever lives here. Empty dwellings wait for future residents, their doors open and their interiors blank and expectant.",
          "paths": [
            "common-hall"
          ]
        }
      },
      "complexityType": "complex",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "factions": [],
      "name": "The Verdant Plot",
      "radius": 5,
      "region": "Heartgate Basin",
      "x": 15,
      "y": 5,
      "basicInfo": "The agricultural and residential heart of the Demi-Plane. When agriculture or settlement development reaches Growing, the Chamberlain leads the creator here — to soil that appeared from nothing and buildings that rose because someone needed shelter. This is where the Demi-Plane starts to feel like it could sustain life rather than merely contain it. Farm fields, a common hall, and residential quarters for oath-sworn residents.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The Verdant Plot's soil is not ordinary earth. It is the Demi-Plane's latent potential made tangible — it grows what the creator and residents need most, not necessarily what they planted. A crop planted out of duty may produce something unexpected. A garden tended with genuine care produces abundantly. The Chamberlain has noticed this pattern but has not mentioned it. They are curious whether the creator will notice on their own.",
      "visited": false,
      "lastVisitedTick": -1,
      "visitedAreas": []
    },
    "Warmvale Springs": {
      "complexityType": "simple",
      "detailType": "basic",
      "name": "Warmvale Springs",
      "radius": 4,
      "region": "Bréanriv Lowlands",
      "x": 15,
      "y": -20,
      "basicInfo": "A hidden hot-spring valley in the southern Lowlands — a narrow gorge where geothermal heat warms a series of natural pools surrounded by wildflowers and soft grass. Warmvale is the Lowlands' answer to Silverfen: less famous, less crowded, and more intimate. The pools are small enough for two or three people, the gorge walls block the wind, and the nearest road is far enough away that the only sounds are water, birdsong, and whatever you bring with you. Adventurers who discover Warmvale tend to keep it secret — not out of selfishness, but because sharing it would ruin the point.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The springs are heated by a pre-Collapse geothermal tap that the ancient civilization used to power something. The tap is still operating, feeding heat into the springs. The thing it was powering is still drawing energy from below. The springs are a side effect of a machine that has not been turned off.",
      "factions": [],
      "areas": {
        "Entrance": {
          "description": "The way into Warmvale Springs.",
