    "Shadowfen Dungeon": {
      "complexityType": "wilderness",
      "detailType": "basic",
      "name": "Shadowfen Dungeon",
      "radius": 4,
      "region": "Scáthfenn",
      "x": 25,
      "y": 0,
      "basicInfo": "A cave system in the eastern fen that opens into underground chambers of carved stone — a pre-Collapse structure that the marsh has been slowly swallowing for centuries. The Dungeon is a D-to-B rank expedition site: the outer chambers are flooded and populated by marsh creatures, the middle chambers are dry and contain useful salvage, and the deep chambers contain things that the marsh-witches advise against disturbing. The Guild posts regular subjugation quests here. The completion rate is decent. The return rate is less so.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The deep chambers connect to the same pre-Collapse network that runs beneath the entire continent. The Shadowfen entrance is one of the few that is still accessible and not actively guarded. Something has been using it to move between regions undetected.",
      "factions": [],
      "visited": false,
      "lastVisitedTick": -1,
      "visitedAreas": []
    },
    "Starfall Clearing": {
      "complexityType": "wilderness",
      "detailType": "basic",
      "name": "Starfall Clearing",
      "radius": 3,
      "region": "Caelvir",
      "x": -25,
      "y": -15,
      "basicInfo": "A crater left by something that fell from the sky centuries ago — now a circular meadow of impossibly vibrant wildflowers ringed by trees that lean inward as if listening. The meteorite at the center has long since been harvested, but the soil it left behind carries a residual magical charge that makes spellcasting here unpredictable and occasionally spectacular. Mages come to experiment; lovers come because the flowers bloom year-round and the starlight here is twice as bright. The clearing is peaceful, strange, and slightly drunk on magic.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The meteorite was not a rock — it was a vessel. Something inside it hatched before the elves arrived and has been living in the forest's spirit ecology ever since, passively amplifying all magic within the clearing.",
      "factions": [],
      "visited": false,
      "lastVisitedTick": -1,
      "visitedAreas": []
    },
    "Wayfarer's Shrine": {
      "complexityType": "simple",
      "detailType": "basic",
      "name": "Wayfarer's Shrine",
      "radius": 3,
      "region": "Fálgarr Marches",
      "x": -10,
      "y": 5,
      "basicInfo": "A small roadside shrine dedicated to a minor goddess of travelers and safe passage — a stone altar, a carved wooden roof, and a tradition of leaving offerings for good luck on the road. The shrine is maintained by a solitary priestess who also sells minor blessing charms and restorative tea to passersby. She asks nothing, expects nothing, and somehow always has exactly what you need. Travelers who leave an offering report unusually good luck on the next leg of their journey.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The goddess is real, and the priestess is her mortal vessel. The goddess is too minor to intervene directly in world events, but she can tip the odds for travelers she likes — and she likes everyone who treats her shrine with respect.",
      "factions": [],
      "visited": false,
      "lastVisitedTick": -1,
      "visitedAreas": []
    },
    "Witchlight Hollow": {
      "complexityType": "simple",
      "detailType": "basic",
      "name": "Witchlight Hollow",
      "radius": 4,
      "region": "Scáthfenn",
      "x": -10,
      "y": -10,
      "basicInfo": "A misty depression in the western marsh where will-o-wisps gather in numbers found nowhere else in Aerfála. The Hollow is also home to a coven of marsh-witches who trade potions, curses, and information with anyone willing to pay their prices — which are never entirely in coin. The witches are not evil, but they are not nice either; they serve the marsh's ecology, and the marsh does not care about human morality. Visitors who treat the Hollow with respect leave with useful alchemical goods and occasionally a love potion that actually works. Visitors who do not respect the Hollow leave changed in ways they did not choose.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The coven's leader is a demon-blooded mage who chose the marsh over the Demon Lord's Army. She is genuinely committed to her coven. She is also genuinely dangerous when crossed. Her love potions work because she puts a piece of herself into every one.",
      "factions": [],
      "visited": false,
      "lastVisitedTick": -1,
      "visitedAreas": []
    },
