    "Ruins of Khad Varr": {
      "complexityType": "wilderness",
      "detailType": "basic",
      "name": "Ruins of Khad Varr",
      "radius": 5,
      "region": "Dúnbheal",
      "x": -25,
      "y": -10,
      "basicInfo": "An abandoned dwarven city sealed two centuries ago after a mining catastrophe — now a B-to-A rank dungeon of collapsed halls, flooded shafts, and automaton guardians that still patrol corridors no one has lived in for generations. Khad Varr's forges were once the finest in Dúnbheal; the ruins still contain masterwork tools and enchanted materials that make the danger worthwhile for well-prepared parties. The entrance is warded but the wards are failing.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The catastrophe was not a mining accident. Khad Varr's crafters broke through into the Old City and made contact with what lives there. The city was sealed to contain what came back up with them. Some of those things are still operational.",
