      "x": 36.10624458405139,
      "y": 13.893755415948608,
      "basicInfo": "A specific mortal frontier town adjacent to the Raiding Grounds. Large enough to be worth raiding; small enough that the garrison is limited. Has survived demon incursions before by a combination of local militia, walls that have been repaired more times than originally built, and the pragmatic calculation that total resistance costs more than negotiated arrangement. The settlement has its own politics: a mayor who leans toward accommodation, a garrison commander who leans toward resistance, a merchant class that does business regardless, and a population with opinions distributed across the full range. Repeated raids create a relationship between the fief and this town whether the player intends it or not.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The garrison commander's second-in-command is the demon agent who feeds information back through the Raiding Grounds network. Has been in position for two years. Is genuinely loyal to the mortal settlement's survival — and genuinely believes that selective cooperation with the fief serves that survival better than total opposition.",
