    "The Grey Fog Wall": {
      "name": "The Grey Fog Wall",
      "basicInfo": "The southern edge of The Grey Boundary — a wall of grey fog stretching horizon to horizon. Cool, damp, opaque. Walking into it feels like walking into nothing: no resistance, no ground change, just a growing sense that forward is not a direction that exists here. Shapes flicker too briefly to name within the fog, and sound carries a half-beat too late. This is the firmest edge of the dimension — it does not expand here, and the fog does not retreat.",
      "x": 20,
      "y": 10,
      "radius": 2,
      "region": "The Grey Boundary",
      "complexityType": "simple",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "The fog is fixed because it anchors the Demi-Plane to a stable point in the dimensional void. If it moved, the dimension's position relative to the mortal world would drift and the Demi-Plane Gate could become unpredictable. The shades within the fog are not hostile — they are half-formed echoes of places the dimension has considered being. Rarely, something genuinely other slips along the wall and is quietly stopped by it.",
      "factions": [],
      "visited": false,
      "lastVisitedTick": -1,
      "visitedAreas": []
    },
    "Anchor Cairn": {
      "name": "Anchor Cairn",
      "basicInfo": "A triple-stacked cairn of pale anchor-stone on the moor — one of several boundary markers the Chamberlain has placed along the southern edge. Each stone is cool, heavy for its size, and utterly still: no moss grows on it, no insect lands on it, no fog condenses on it. A small shimenawa rope ties the top stone. From here the fog wall can be watched safely.",
      "x": 50,
      "y": 35,
      "radius": 1,
      "region": "The Grey Boundary",
      "complexityType": "simple",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "Anchor-stone is condensed dimensional fixedness — literalized stability, which is why it stays unmarked by moss, insects, or fog. An older cairn stands nearby that predates the Chamberlain: its stones are arranged in a pattern matching no tradition he knows, and it hums faintly when the fog wall ripples. He has never claimed it and suspects it was not built by hands at all.",
      "factions": [],
