    },
    "The Last Edge": {
      "name": "The Last Edge",
      "basicInfo": "The barren rim of the Demi-Plane — smooth flat stony ground, motionless air, steady grey light, extending to the dimension's end in the southeast. No shadows fall here; light comes from nowhere and everywhere at once. The plain is broken by nothing: no grass, no stones out of place, no sound. Walking its length is walking beside the fact that everything ends.",
      "x": 15,
      "y": 35,
      "radius": 4,
      "region": "The Last Edge",
      "complexityType": "wilderness",
      "detailType": "basic",
      "known": true,
      "hiddenInfo": "The Edge is barren on purpose — the dimension holds its outermost ground in perfect rest so the anchor point beneath it never drifts. Discoveries here are rare and always significant: nullstone deposits, grey crystal seams, fixed-point fragments, strange geometric formations, or remnants — worn and impossible — that predate the dimension itself. The Chamberlain quietly collects anything found and records it in a ledger he keeps in his quarters.",
