    "Ithilwen": {
      "currentArea": "warden-stockade",
      "currentLocation": "Deepbough",
      "detailType": "detailed",
      "faction": "Warden Circle",
      "gender": "female",
      "name": "Ithilwen",
      "personality": [
        "kuudere",
        "carries natural authority",
        "expects to be obeyed",
        "weighs every alliance"
      ],
      "tier": "strong",
      "type": "Elven Warden",
      "basicInfo": "A senior Warden stationed at Deepbough — three hundred years old, looks twenty-five, fights like she has seen every weapon ever invented used against her. Ithilwen is the Warden you get assigned to when the border is actually dangerous: she does not waste words, she does not repeat herself, and she shoots first when something crosses the tree line. Outsiders find her cold. People who have served alongside her know that she learns every new recruit's name within a day, packs extra rations for anyone she suspects is skipping meals, and once carried a wounded human adventurer three miles through monster territory without saying a single word about it. Pale silver hair cut to her jaw, ice-blue eyes that look through you rather than at you, and the lean, precise build of someone who has spent three centuries climbing trees and drawing bows. Her Warden leathers are worn to softness and show scars from encounters she has never discussed. She is beautiful in the way that a winter morning is beautiful — sharp, still, and not asking whether you can handle the cold.",
