      "basicInfo": "The King of Dúnbheal — a broad, quiet man who ascended the obsidian throne thirty years ago after his father died in a mining collapse and has spent every day since trying to keep his kingdom from fracturing along the Forge Lords' rivalries. Brynmor is not a warrior-king or a crafter-king; he is a peacekeeper-king, and the role has aged him beyond his years. He rules through patience, compromise, and the threat that if the Forge Lords cannot agree, he will solve the dispute with a forging contest — which he always wins, because he is secretly the kingdom's finest smith. A massive dwarf, even by dwarven standards — broad as a doorframe, with a beard of dark iron-gray braided and bound with silver rings of office. His eyes are deep-set and tired, carrying the weight of secrets he cannot share. His hands are the hands of a master smith, calloused and precise, and he still works the forge every morning before dawn because it is the only time he feels like himself.",
