      "tier": "average",
      "type": "Academy Student",
      "basicInfo": "A first-year human scholarship student — earnest, hardworking, and so genuinely kind that half the campus suspects it is an act. It is not. Tomás grew up on a farm in the Bréanriv Lowlands, tested into the Academy on raw magical talent, and has spent every day since being quietly overwhelmed by the scale of everything around him. He is not naive — he knows nobles play games and that the world is not fair — he just refuses to let that change how he treats people.\n\nHe is the student who helps carry luggage, shares notes without being asked, and remembers everyone's name even after one introduction. His magic is earth-element, which he uses to tend the Academy gardens in his spare time. The groundskeeper has started leaving him tasks. Broad-shouldered, sun-browned, and built like someone who has been doing manual labor since he could walk. Dark hair cropped short for practicality, warm brown eyes that crinkle when he smiles — which is often — and hands that are calloused from both spellwork and garden tools. He wears the standard Academy uniform without modification and looks slightly uncomfortable in it, like a farmer dressed for church. His smile is the kind that makes you smile back whether you intended to or not.",
      "hiddenInfo": "Tomás's magical aptitude is not just raw talent — it is a hereditary gift from a bloodline he does not know about. His grandmother was a dragon-blooded who abandoned her heritage to marry a farmer, and the draconic trace has been dormant for two generations. It is beginning to wake. His earth magic is developing unexplained heat properties, and his strength has been increasing beyond what training accounts for. If it manifests fully, his anonymous life at the Academy ends.",
