      "basicInfo": "The Ambitious General — the other commander who waited outside the vault. Was in correspondence with a rival noble house during the interregnum. Has not been caught. Is now performing loyalty with the specific energy of someone who has decided that the new ruler is more valuable as an ally than as a stepping stone. May actually be right. The Demon Prince-Princess's read on this NPC will shape a significant portion of the fief's political arc. Lean demon with indigo skin and four small horns arranged in a crown pattern. Immaculate uniform. Moves like someone who is always calculating the next three steps. Smiles precisely when expected.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The correspondence with the rival house was not about betraying the bloodline — it was about ensuring the fief's survival if the egg never hatched. Sathia made contingency plans the way a competent general makes contingency plans. Whether those plans have been fully abandoned now that the ruler has emerged is a question even Sathia has not fully answered. Additionally, she has identified two orders from the Demon Lord that she cannot reconcile with any military objective she understands. She is waiting for a third before she decides anything. She does not believe she is disloyal. She believes she is conducting due diligence. A player who reaches A-rank equivalent standing and demonstrates competence and discretion may earn a formal mutual-intelligence arrangement — not fealty in the standard sense, but a partnership that may develop depending on the Demon Lord's next order and what the player does when it arrives.",
