      "basicInfo": "The chief archivist of the Verdant Archive — an elf of approximately three hundred years who has spent the last hundred of them organizing, cross-referencing, and silently judging the contents of the restricted root collection. Loris speaks softly, makes precise notes with a quill he has used for sixty years, and considers loud voices in the library to be a personal affront. He is helpful to visiting scholars within strict procedural limits and absolutely refuses to discuss the restricted collection with anyone who has not signed the appropriate forms. Slight, even by elven standards, with long pale-blonde hair tied back severely and silver-grey eyes that look through anyone who has not earned his trust. He wears archivist robes in muted forest-green with deep pockets full of notebooks. His fingers are stained with ink. He has a habit of touching the spines of books he passes — a brief, almost reverent acknowledgment that he is unaware he does.",
