    "Sir Kaelen the Disgraced": {
      "currentArea": "",
      "currentLocation": "The Pale Steppes",
      "gender": "female",
      "name": "Sir Kaelen the Disgraced",
      "personality": [
        "honourable",
        "bitter",
        "protective",
        "self-punishing"
      ],
      "tier": "strong",
      "type": "Human Noble",
      "basicInfo": "A former knight of Solasreach who was stripped of rank and title after refusing an order she considered dishonourable. She did not argue — she simply laid down her sword and walked away, which the court found more infuriating than defiance would have been. Now she lives on the Pale Steppes, helping the scattered settlements as a nameless defender. She fights like someone who has nothing left to prove and everything left to protect. Encounters the player as an adversary first — she mistakes the player for a threat to the locals and attacks before talking. Tall woman with close-cropped dark hair and a scar across her cheek from the duel that ended her career. Wears plain leathers with no heraldry. Carries a longsword she still maintains meticulously. Moves like someone who has spent years trying to be invisible and failed.",
      "hiddenInfo": "The order she refused was to execute a child of demon blood. She has never told anyone this. The child now lives in a border village, unaware that a stranger ensured their survival. Kaelen does not think of this as heroism. She thinks of it as the bare minimum, and she is furious that the bare minimum cost her everything.",
